      "sphere of radius R₀:\n   K dA integrand =  sin(u)    — R₀ has cancelled already\n   ∫K dA =  4*%pi\n   χ = ∫K dA / 2π =  2    ✓  χ(S²) = 2\ntorus of revolution, tube 1, centre 2:\n   K dA integrand =  (cos(u)^2+2*cos(u))/sqrt(cos(u)^2+4*cos(u)+4)\n                       (= K · dA = cos u/(2+cos u) · (2+cos u))\n   ∫K dA =  0\n   χ = 0  ✓.  4.06 found K positive on the outside and negative on\n   the inside; this says they cancel EXACTLY, which topology forces\n   and no reshaping of the tube can disturb.\nellipsoid of revolution, semi-axes (1,1,2):\n   integrand at v = 0 :\n                        (4*sin(u)^2)/((3*sin(u)^2+1)\n                                     *sqrt(3*sin(u)^4+sin(u)^2))\n   independent of v, so ∫dv contributes 2π.\n   ∫₀^π … du =  2.0    (estimated error  4.0928854088543486e-12 )\n   χ = 2π·that/2π =  2.0    ✓  still 2\nK is not constant on the ellipsoid — larger at the poles, smaller at\nthe equator — and the integral does not notice.  That is what a\ncharacteristic class is: a number no deformation of the geometry can\nchange, only a change of topology.\nclosed hyperbolic surfaces (4.07): area = 2π|χ| with K = −1, so\n   ∫K dA / 2π = −area/2π = χ\n      genus  2  : area  12.566370614359172    ∫K dA/2π =  -2    χ =  -2\n      genus  3  : area  25.132741228718345    ∫K dA/2π =  -4    χ =  -4\n      genus  4  : area  37.69911184307752    ∫K dA/2π =  -6    χ =  -6"
